law=E-SAP-0036 IOM4 lane mirror at 0x40054000 (retires the E-SAP-0035 boot pins below; every new pin is a two-run byte-identical pair re-taken on the final tree)
startup_stop=budget pc=0x000e1862 instructions=89441684 virtual_time_ns=30000000000 (100M/30s budget, guest WFI park, run_pair_sha256=98e1a162bb2b33348bf86b17d1dd0fb7fffad076dac5dbbc52376c643161361b)
startup_stop_300s=budget pc=0x000a6c06 instructions=100000000 virtual_time_ns=85159974844 (100M/300s, instruction budget first, 234 ns earlier than the retired pin because the command write no longer takes the fault vector, run_pair_sha256=dc35696dd307c7b3c7c326ff8fa1296bce8839c5f19d15ec29d9efe5da362fe5)
wake_alarm_irq=E-SAP-0035: IRQ2 rises at every whole-second alarm occurrence (RPT=Second, ALML=0, clock epoch 1970-01-01), first wake at virtual_time_ns=1000000000; pinned by tests/devices/test_sapporo_rtc.c (test_second_alarm_law)
iom4_command_path=E-SAP-0036: the first IOM4 command write 0x38000212 (read, device 0x28, offset 3, size 2) is served by the mirror instead of faulting; the guest reaches the observed 0x28 device and the 0x36 MAX17050 gauge, whose received gauge word 0xc000 (expecting-fold of the probe-pinned map) is readable at 0x100 and 0x108; law probes /tmp/sap235/iom4law{,2,3,4,5,6}.resc, sixteen to eighteen readouts each, run pairs byte-identical (sha256 5a2f3974..., ea5feadd2042fe3884a7240eaba28e6f0ec9436049d461376eb480a09530dcee)
boot_window_1b125s=budget pc=0x000e1862 instructions=104283521 virtual_time_ns=125000000000 (1B/125s: the whole former ~120.148 s window now runs to the time budget with no machine reset at all, run_pair_sha256=1c9e9ce0668c5951f1291941d08d67646fb388d6ec054d046a438eb07a936d97)
boot_cycle_1b300s=stop=budget pc=0x000e1862 instructions=122878688 virtual_time_ns=300000000000 (1B/300s; no machine-reset-request line, the --trace logs are empty in both runs, run_pair_sha256=3f6e0818a4ba15a39c56299f6da22b30e49ed4ee1e56905a4d6c4b9d8771c938, trace_pair_sha256=e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855)
boot_passes_3x30s=89441684 then 85778971 then 85778979 instructions, every pass stop=budget(reason=2) pc=0xe1862 virtual_time_ns=30000000000 (machine-API semu_machine_reset loop; the three counts are uniformly +162 over the retired E-SAP-0035 record, pair sha256=2cae3ad5eae6a38736edcae1f2149b7533478b3201b64315f5b52c9033d0f5d0)
reset_request_pc=0x000cdf5a (guest AIRCR helper; not reached in any 300 s window any more, because the ~120.148 s cadence was the IOM4 BusFault and not guest policy)
retired_pins=E-SAP-0035: startup_stop instructions=89441522 (pair 8d4f5694...), startup_stop_300s pc=0x000a7022 virtual_time_ns=85159975078 (pair 9100c14b...), boot_cycle_1b300s machine-reset-request t=120150672935 and t=240298801495 (period 120148128560 ns, pc=0x000cdf5a lr=0xffffffed xpsr=0x21000003) with stop instructions=299057602 virtual_time_ns=300310661417 (pair 932fecab...), and the machine-API passes 89441522/85778809/85778817; that ~120.148 s AIRCR cadence was the BusFault (cfsr=0x8200) on the first IOM4 command write 0x38000212 at the unmirrored 0x40054000 window, so these numbers are superseded by the lane mirror and are not era drift (volatile logs; new pair hashes recorded above and in docs/migration-evidence.md E-SAP-0036)

[limitations]
cache_interventions=unknown
logical_storage_interventions=unknown
description=Component contracts are exact; the live RTC dispatch (this profile only) implements the lane Timers.AmbiqApollo4_RTC register law since E-SAP-0035: WRTC-gated CNTL/CNTU pair commits the epoch clock, RPT drives the alarm cadence, IRQ2 = Enable && Status until InterruptClear. Since E-SAP-0036 the IOM4 window at 0x40054000 of the same profile is served by the lane-mirror engine in src/devices/sapporo_iom4.c: 8-word FIFO rings with the threshold law at 0x100-0x114, command and command-status at 0x120/0x128/0x12c, interrupts 0x200-0x20c, the DMA engine 0x210-0x248 with its target gate, and the device-config 0x2c4 gate that admits the observed 0x28 device and the 0x36 MAX17050 gauge. Both former fault drivers of the boot are now gone: the W +0x20 refusal (E-SAP-0034 ~1.01186 s cycle) and the BusFault on the first IOM4 command write (the ~120.148 s AIRCR cycle). The guest runs uninterrupted through 300 s of virtual time, wakes at whole-second alarm occurrences, and parks in WFI at pc 0x000e1862; what it does beyond that park (122878688 instructions in 300 s) is next-census territory. 2.22/2.33/2.39 keep the inert RTC stub and the shared E-A4-IOM-001 IOM law unchanged, because the mirror is created only behind the sapporo-2.35.34 profile gate. Offsets the lane leaves unobserved (0x50, 0x115..0x119, 0x230, 0x238), the POPWR/POPT controls, and non-4 widths stay fail-closed refusals - the boot provokes none of them, which the empty --trace logs of both 300 s runs show; the live IOM4 and RTC module state is not carried in vmstate, so a snapshot resume reads it as zero, as with the RTC
